    B4-Q3 control (fluid feels Phi_b itself, S_int = -Int rho_c Phi_b): lambda' = G M_c/r^2 -> a_react = -G M_c/r^2 (inward extra pull);  EL residual = 0
  [PASS] C2a (sympy) reciprocity theorem: baryons feel a_react = -grad lambda, lap lambda = -4 pi G q; for S_int = Int F^ij T_ij, a_react = 8 pi G [F_perp' + (F_perp-F_rr)/r]; reproduces B4-Q3 (-G M_c/r^2 for kappa = 1)
         Cartesian identity residual 1.8e-15; EL residuals 0, 0
    healthy-kinetic-term (Z>0) formulation without a multiplier: a_react = (eps c/Z) x 8 pi G[...] = C x 8 pi G[...] with C = c eps/Z the FLUID-side coupling; G_eff on baryons is renormalised by eps^2/Z (removable with Z -> infinity) but the reaction is NOT.
  [PASS] C2b the reaction depends only on the fluid-side coupling C = c eps/Z: no choice of normalisation of Phi_b removes it
         a_react coefficient = c*epsilon/Z = C

